I took the 32x32 tileset distributed on nethack.org for Windows NetHack
and did the 30 seconds of work needed to convert it to the XPM format
usable with NetHack for Linux or UNIX with X11 support.  (The work was
loading up the Windows BMP file, cropping it to 1280x864 to remove an
unused region of black pixels, and saving it as an XPM file.)

You can download the result (approximately 155K zipped) from

http://hexadecimal.uoregon.edu/~stevev/tiles32x.zip

The unzipped tiles32.xpm is about 1.1Mbytes in size.  You can use it
instead of the standard tileset by changing the X resource:

NetHack.tile_file: /path/to/tiles32.xpm

